use std
into hair.amni

Imports: os, binary, gfx, math, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.motion and gfx.scene3d. This file is a module with no main.

Struct `HairU` holds view_proj, view and proj (each `gfx::mat4`), then size, cam, to_sun, sun_rgb, hair, sky, params and look (each `float4`), then light_vp (`gfx::mat4`), light (`float4`) and shadow_vp (`gfx::mat4`), in that order, matching the GLSL uniform block `Hair` in shaders/strand_common.glsl.

Module state: `var on = false`, `var guides = 0`, `var parts = 0`, `var cells = 0`, `var sdf_done = false`, `var sim_reset = true`, `var probe_ask = false`, `var probe_v f32[>..]` (eight probe results), `var hm_prev = gfx::mat4_identity`, `var part_node int[>..]` (global glTF node of each collision part), `var part_ib gfx::mat4[>..]` (its inverse bind matrix), `var simv float4[>..]` (the simulation table, 116 entries, laid out as the `Sim` buffer of shaders/strand_body.glsl), `var tgt`, `var st`, `var gd`, `var simb`, `var sdfb`, `var trib`, `var statb` (`gfx::Buffer`), `sim_p`, `sdf_p` (`gfx::ComputePipeline`), `var w = 0`, `var h = 0`, `var spc = 96`, `var points = 0`, `var segments = 0`, `var center = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `var bones = 0` (spring-bone count), `var bone_node int[>..]` (glTF node index of each bone, local to the asset), `var mats gfx::mat4[>..]` (one matrix per bone), and `var` handles `pts`, `rest`, `skin`, `matsb`, `segs`, `front`, `acc`, `lfront`, `lacc` (`gfx::Buffer`), `hairt` (`gfx::Texture`), `smp` (`gfx::Sampler`), `comp` (`gfx::Pipeline`), `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p`, `skin_p` (`gfx::ComputePipeline`, what `gfx::compute_pipeline` returns, assigned directly), each starting from `default<T>()`.

`hair_size(nw int, nh int)` sets w and h and (re)creates the screen-sized resources: with `rw = gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ`, `front = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 4, [])`, `acc = gfx::buffer(rw, nw * nh * 64, [])` and `hairt = gfx::texture(gfx::TextureDesc { format: gfx::RGBA16F, usage: gfx::SAMPLED | gfx::COMPUTE_WRITE, width: nw as i32, height: nh as i32 })` (gfx::buffer always takes three arguments; an empty slice zero-fills).

`hair_open(path const byte[:], nw int, nh int, strands int) bool` reads the guides file with the unqualified `read_file(path, data)` into a `byte[>..]` (false: return false). Layout: 4 magic bytes, "HMG2" or "HMG3" (byte 3 is 50 or 51), then little-endian i32 guides, points, segments at bytes 4, 8, 12 (read with `binary::gather(data, at, 4) as int`), then points × 48 bytes, then segments × 16 bytes; an HMG3 file then has an i32 bone count `bones` at `e = 16 + points * 48 + segments * 16`, `bones` i32 node indices after it (append each to `bone_node`), then points × 16 bytes of skin data starting at `k = e + 4 + bones * 4`. Set `points`, `segments`, `spc = strands`; `pts = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `tgt` the same way (the animated targets), `st = gfx::buffer(<same usage>, points * 32, [])` (simulated positions and previous positions), `segs = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, segments * 16, <the segment bytes>)`. When `bones > 0`: `rest = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 48, data[16..16 + points * 48])`, `skin = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, points * 16, data[k..k + points * 16])`, resize `mats` to `bones` entries of `gfx::mat4_identity`, `matsb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, bones * 64, [])` and `skin_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_skin.comp"))`. `center` is the mean of the first three f32 of every point (point k at byte 16 + k*48, each `binary::f32_from_bits(binary::gather(data, at, 4) as! u32)`). Light buffers: `lfront = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 4, [])`, `lacc = gfx::buffer(rw, 512 * 512 * 64, [])`. `smp = gfx::sampler(gfx::NEAREST, gfx::CLAMP)`; `comp = gfx::pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.vert"), embed_shader("shaders/strand_comp.frag"), gfx::PipelineDesc { blend: gfx::BLEND_PREMULTIPLIED })`; `clear_p`, `raster_p`, `resolve_p` with `gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader(...))` of "shaders/strand_clear.comp", "shaders/strand_raster.comp", "shaders/strand_resolve.comp". Guides: walk the segments in order (segment s has its point index at byte `16 + points * 48 + s * 16` and its guide number 4 bytes later); a new guide starts at the first segment and whenever the guide number differs from the previous segment's, with first point that segment's point and count 2, and every further segment of the same guide adds 1 to the count. Keep them as four i32 per guide in an `i32[>..]` list (first point, point count, skinned flag, 0), where the skinned flag is 1 when the file has bones and some point k of the guide has skin weights (the f32 at bytes `k * 16 + 8` and `k * 16 + 12` of the skin data, decoded with `binary::f32_from_bits`) adding up to more than 0.001, else 0. Set `guides` to the count, `gd = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, guides * 16, bytes_of(<that list>))`, `statb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, guides * 16, [])`, `simb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, 116 * 16, [])`, resize `simv` to 116 zero `float4`s and `probe_v` to 8 zeros, `sim_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_sim.comp"))` and `sdf_p = gfx::compute_pipeline(embed_shader("shaders/strand_sdf.comp"))`. Until `hair_body` runs, `sdfb` and `trib` are `gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, 16, [])` placeholders. Call `hair_size(nw, nh)`, set `on = true`, return true.

`skin_joint(sk int, node int) int` returns the k below `gltf::skins[sk].joints.count` with `gltf::ints[gltf::skins[sk].joints.first + k] == node`, or -1.

`tri_owner(v0 int, v1 int, v2 int) int` returns the skin joint with the largest weight summed over the three global vertices' four influences: keep parallel lists `js int[>..]` and `ws f32[>..]`; for each vertex v and c in 0..3, `j = gltf::verts[v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 18 + c] as int` and `w = gltf::verts[v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS + 22 + c]`, add w to the entry of j (pushing a new entry when j is not yet listed); return the j with the largest summed weight (-1 when the lists are empty).

`tri_box_hit(tl const float4[:], k int, lo float3, hi float3) bool` is true when the box of triangle k (the xyz of `tl[3k]`, `tl[3k + 1]`, `tl[3k + 2]`) padded by 0.035 on every side overlaps the box from lo to hi.

`hair_body(asset int)` builds the collision body: one signed distance grid per body part, each rigid with one skin joint, in the skin's bind space (the space the strands are stored in). Return when `!on`. Let `n0 = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.first` and `nc = gltf::assets[asset].nodes.count`; `sn = gltf::find_node(asset, "skin")`; return when `sn < 0 || gltf::nodes[sn].mesh < 0 || gltf::nodes[sn].skin < 0`; `sk = gltf::nodes[sn].skin`.
Parts: `var pj int[>..]`; for each name in the list "head", "neck_01", "spine_03", "spine_02", "clavicle_l", "clavicle_r", "upperarm_l", "upperarm_r": `nd = gltf::find_node(asset, name)`; when `nd >= 0` and `k = skin_joint(sk, nd)` is `>= 0`, push nd to `part_node`, `gltf::matrices[gltf::skins[sk].inverse_binds.first + k]` to `part_ib` and k to `pj`. `parts = part_node.len`.
Boxes: `var lo float3[>..]` and `var hi float3[>..]`, one per part, starting at `float3 { 1e9, 1e9, 1e9 }` and `float3 { -1e9, -1e9, -1e9 }`.
Triangles: `var all float4[>..]`. For each n from n0 to n0 + nc - 1 with `gltf::nodes[n].mesh >= 0` and `gltf::nodes[n].skin == sk`, let `mn = gltf::text_of(gltf::meshes[gltf::nodes[n].mesh].name)`; skip unless mn is "skin", "face", "scalp" or "tank". For each primitive index q from `gltf::meshes[m].prims.first` for `.prims.count` (with `pr = gltf::prims[q]`) and each t below `pr.icount / 3`: `v0`, `v1`, `v2` are `pr.vfirst + gltf::indices[pr.ifirst + 3 * t + c] as int` for c = 0, 1, 2; positions `pa`, `pb`, `pc` are the floats 0..2 at `v * gltf::VERTEX_FLOATS`. `j = tri_owner(v0, v1, v2)`; `ow` = the index i in pj with `pj[i] == j`, or -1. Push `float4 { pa.x, pa.y, pa.z, ow as f32 }`, `float4 { pb.x, pb.y, pb.z, 0.0 }`, `float4 { pc.x, pc.y, pc.z, 0.0 }` to `all`; when `ow >= 0` grow `lo[ow]` and `hi[ow]` (component min and max) by pa, pb and pc.
Grids: `var tl float4[>..]`; `cells = 0`; for each part p: `o = 20 + 12 * p`. When `lo[p].x < hi[p].x`: `a = lo[p] - float3 { 0.035, 0.035, 0.035 }`, `b = hi[p] + float3 { 0.035, 0.035, 0.035 }`, `sz = b - a`, `cell = max(0.007, max(sz.x, max(sz.y, sz.z)) / 63.0)`, `gx = (sz.x / cell) as int + 2` and likewise gy, gz; `t0 = tl.len / 3`; for each triangle k below `all.len / 3` with `tri_box_hit(all[..], k, a, b)` push its three entries to `tl`. Otherwise `a = float3 { 0.0, 0.0, 0.0 }`, `cell = 0.007`, gx = gy = gz = 2 and `t0 = tl.len / 3`. Then `simv[o] = float4 { a.x, a.y, a.z, cell }`, `simv[o + 1] = float4 { gx as f32, gy as f32, gz as f32, cells as f32 }`, `simv[o + 2] = float4 { t0 as f32, (tl.len / 3 - t0) as f32, 0.0, 0.0 }` and `cells += gx * gy * gz`.
Finally `simv[8].w = parts as f32`, `simv[14] = float4 { cells as f32, 0.0005, 0.004, 1.0 }`, `trib = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ, max(tl.len, 1) * 16, bytes_of(tl))`, `sdfb = gfx::buffer(gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_READ | gfx::BUFFER_COMPUTE_WRITE, max(cells, 1) * 8, [])`, `sdf_done = false`, and print "hair body: " parts " parts, " cells " cells, " tl.len / 3 " triangles".

`hair_probe(k int) f32` asks for a probe of the simulation and answers from the last one: it sets `probe_ask = true` and returns `probe_v[k]` when k is 0..7, else 0. The probe values are 0 points inside the body (not counting roots), 1 roots inside the body, 2 mean tip distance from the styled target in millimeters, 3 the largest tip distance, 4 the mean sideways (x) tip offset in millimeters, 5 the number of probes taken, 6 guides.

`hair_bone(i int) int` returns `bone_node[i]`, and `hair_pose(i int, m gfx::mat4)` sets `mats[i] = m` (a bone's motion, in the head's rest space) when `i` is in range.

`hair_draw(model gfx::mat4, dt f32)` simulates the strands for a frame of dt seconds and draws them (stored in the head's rest space) moved by `model`, onto `s3d::hdr_target()`; call it between `s3d::render_begin()` and `s3d::render_end(...)`. Return when `!on`. Let `im = linalg::inverse(model)`. Fill `var u = default<HairU>()`: view_proj `gfx::mul(s3d::view_proj_nj, model)`, view `gfx::mul(s3d::view_mat, model)`, proj `s3d::proj_mat`; size (w, h, spc, segments, all `as f32`); cam: `e = linalg::point(im, s3d::view.eye)` as (e.x, e.y, e.z, 0.7); to_sun: `t = gfx::mul(im, float4 { s3d::sun.to_sun.x, s3d::sun.to_sun.y, s3d::sun.to_sun.z, 0.0 })`, `ld = linalg::unit3(float3 { t.x, t.y, t.z })`, stored as (ld, 0); sun_rgb `s3d::sun.rgb` with w 0; hair (0.58, 0.38, 0.14, 0.42); sky (0.12, 0.13, 0.15, 40.0); params (0.004, 1.7, 0.004, 0.00007); look (1.0, 6.0, 0.0, 0.7); light_vp `gfx::mul(gfx::perspective(0.24, 1.0, 2.0, 4.0), gfx::look_at(center + ld * 3.0, center, float3 { 0.0, 1.0, 0.0 }))`; light (512, 512, 0.35, 256 / tan(0.12)) all `as f32`; shadow_vp `gfx::mul(s3d::cascade_vp[0], model)`. Each compute pass: `gfx::begin_compute(...)`, `gfx::bind(pipeline)`, set `u.look.z` to the mode, `gfx::uniforms(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, u)`, ..., `gfx::end_compute()`. A nested `fn raster(rw0 gfx::Buffer, rw1 gfx::Buffer, ro0 gfx::Buffer, ro1 gfx::Buffer, mode int)` runs one raster pass: read-write [rw0, rw1], raster_p, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 0, s3d::nd_target(), smp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::COMPUTE, 1, s3d::shadow_map, smp)`, storage buffers 0..3 = pts, segs, ro0, ro1, dispatch ((segments + 63) / 64, spc, 1). Order: first, when `bones > 0`, skin the strand targets: `gfx::update_buffer(matsb, 0, bytes_of(mats)[..bones * 64])`, then a compute pass with read-write buffers [tgt], skin_p, `u.size.w = points as f32` before its `gfx::uniforms`, storage buffers 0..2 = rest, skin, matsb, dispatch ((points + 63) / 64, 1, 1), and set `u.size.w = segments as f32` back after it. Then simulate: let `reset = sim_reset || dt <= 0.0 || length3(model.c3.xyz - hm_prev.c3.xyz) > 0.5`; when reset set `hm_prev = model`. Fill `simv`: entries 0..3 the columns c0..c3 of `model`, 4..7 those of `im`, `simv[8] = float4 { dt, if reset { 1.0 } else { 0.0 }, 0.0, parts as f32 }`, `simv[9] = float4 { 0.0, -9.81, 0.0, guides as f32 }`, 10..13 the columns of `hm_prev`, `simv[15] = float4 { 0.012, 0.35, 0.08, 0.5 }` (shape stiffness at the tip and at the root, then the same for guides on spring bones), `simv[16] = float4 { 0.5, 0.9, 0.0, 0.02 }` (bend stiffness, length-correction damping, unused, velocity damping); for each part p with `o = 20 + 12 p` and `mp = gfx::mul(motion::world[part_node[p]], part_ib[p])`, entries `o + 3 .. o + 6` the columns of `linalg::inverse(mp)` and `o + 7 .. o + 10` those of `mp`. `gfx::update_buffer(simb, 0, bytes_of(simv))`. When `!sdf_done && cells > 0`, build the distance grids once: a compute pass with read-write buffers [sdfb], sdf_p, storage buffers 0..1 = trib, simb, dispatch ((cells + 63) / 64, 1, 1), and set `sdf_done = true`. Then a compute pass with read-write buffers [st, pts, statb], sim_p, storage buffers 0..3 = tgt, gd, simb, sdfb, dispatch ((guides + 63) / 64, 1, 1). Set `sim_reset = false` and `hm_prev = model`. When `probe_ask`: read the per-guide results with `gfx::read_buffer(statb, 0, raw[..])` into a `byte[>..]` `raw` of guides * 16 bytes; with four little-endian u32 per guide (`binary::gather(raw, at, 4)`), set `probe_v[0]` to the sum of the first, `probe_v[1]` the sum of the second, `probe_v[2]` the mean of the third divided by 1000, `probe_v[3]` the largest third divided by 1000, `probe_v[4]` the mean of (the fourth minus 1000000000) divided by 1000 (all as f32), add 1 to `probe_v[5]`, set `probe_v[6] = guides as f32` and `probe_ask = false`. Then clear [front, acc] mode 0 dispatching ((w*h + 63) / 64, 1, 1); clear [lfront, lacc] mode 2 dispatching ((512*512 + 63) / 64, 1, 1); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 2); raster(lfront, lacc, front, acc, 3); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 0); raster(front, acc, lfront, lacc, 1); resolve with buffers [] and textures [hairt] (two-list `gfx::begin_compute`), resolve_p, mode 1, storage buffer 0 = acc, dispatch ((w + 7) / 8, (h + 7) / 8, 1); then `if gfx::begin_pass(gfx::PassDesc { color: [s3d::hdr_target(), gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}, gfx::Texture{0}], clear_color: false, .. })` { `gfx::bind(comp)`, `gfx::bind_texture(gfx::FRAGMENT, 0, hairt, smp)`, `gfx::draw(3)`, `gfx::end_pass()` }.
